# Trivy suppressions for this repo (intentional, documented). Each ID appears in
# both forms: the AVD- prefix older Trivy versions report and the bare ID newer
# ones do.

# GCP-0066 (tfstate bucket without a customer-managed encryption key), in
# specs/requirements/gcp: the bucket uses Google-managed encryption. A CMEK
# needs a KMS key ring and key that the installation owns and rotates, which
# this module cannot create on its own. Access is what protects the state
# (uniform bucket-level access, public access prevention, object admin only
# for the worker's principal), as the README's "The tfstate is a credential
# store" section says.
AVD-GCP-0066
GCP-0066

# DS-0026 (no HEALTHCHECK in the Dockerfile): the image runs as an ephemeral
# worker pod that the nullplatform agent starts, talks to and reaps; there is
# no long-lived server in it to probe, and Kubernetes ignores Docker
# HEALTHCHECK anyway.
AVD-DS-0026
DS-0026

# Not suppressed on purpose: the Go CVEs in usr/local/bin/tofu. They are in
# libraries compiled into the OpenTofu release binary (go-jose, x/mod, x/net,
# grpc) and go away only with a newer OpenTofu release; keep them visible so a
# TOFU_VERSION bump is the reminder.
